{
 "priority": 7,
 "source_bins": [
  "talk.bin"
 ],
 "strings": {
  "Well, their apartment complex had an empty unit where all of them were living. Their key was even in the mailbox.": "",
  "Apparently that unit was \"stigmatized property\" so they slipped in without anyone noticing.": "",
  "Huh, hadn't considered that. I'm surprised you found them.": "",
  "That's what the evidence pointed to, and there they were.": "",
  "You're quite the detective, Kamaguchi-san.": "",
  "Heh. Coming from an actual detective, I'm quite flattered.": "",
  "Oh, Yagami-san. Came here to kill some time?": "",
  "More or less. Anything interesting happen lately?": "",
  "Actually, I was just talking about this customer who came in a little while ago. Total doofus, that guy.": "",
  "Comes right in and asks if he can borrow a million yen.": "",
  "For what?": "",
  "Wanted to give his girlfriend an anniversary present. Said he wanted to rent out an entire host club for her party.": "",
  "That's... pretty odd.": "",
  "Right? Apparently his idea of showing his girl a good time is letting her flirt with a bunch of fake-ass prettyboys.": "",
  "\"Nothing's too expensive for my pretty little pudding.\" Yeah, sure. I almost told him to get a grip when he said it.": "",
  "(That sounds oddly familiar... Or maybe it's just my imagination.)": "",
  "So did you end up lending him the money?": "",
  "Hell no. How could I lend money to a moron like that? Didn't look like he had enough to pay back the loan anyway.": "",
  "Hah. Smart move.": "",
  "Ah, there you are. Looks like the Keihin Gang got rid of the bounty on your head.": "",
  "Yeah, thanks to you guys. Really appreciate it.": "",
  "Hey, we owed you one. Simple as that.": "",
  "They ended up running away like cowards, didn't they?": "",
  "Yep. They were quick to pick a fight and even quicker to flee.": "",
  "I heard you shut down the illegal gun trade. Hopefully Kamurocho's a bit safer from now on.": "",
  "Yeah, I hope so.": "",
  "What's up, Yagami-san? Need some debt counseling?": "",
  "Not at the moment, at least.": "",
  "You sure? You could always start with a smaller loan and work your way up.": "",
  "Yeah, and I'm sure you'll flip out as soon as you realize I can't pay it back.": "",
  "Would a true friend default on a debt, though? I think not.": "",
  "Then consider me a stranger and I'll take your little offer.": "",
  "Hey, don't be a cheapskate. Guess I should've known better, huh?": "",
  "By the way, Yagami-san. Are you dating anyone right now?": "",
  "Why? Isn't it obvious?": "",
  "Hey, Tabuchi, aren't you getting a little too familiar with him? I thought you were a married woman.": "",
  "Well, there's always room for dessert... and this one looks extra sweet. So my question still stands.": "",
  "...Umm. Check, please?": "",
  "Hahaha! Hear that? Guess he's not on the menu!": "",
  "How disappointing...": "",
  "Oh, how's it going, Yagami-san? Business as usual?": "",
  "Something like that. You?": "",
  "About the same, and that's just how I prefer it.": "",
  "There'd be something wrong with the world if there was a line out the door for people coming to see <font_kind=yakuza_italic>me</font_kind>.": "",
  "Heh, coming from a moneylender, I guess that makes sense.": "",
  "Hey, Yagami-san. Think I can count on you to do some collections for me? Only when there's trouble, of course.": "",
  "When you've been in business as long as I have, you learn how to guess a person's income just by looking at 'em.": "",
  "You serious?": "",
  "Yeah, for example, I'm guessing you make... about...": "",
  "Hey Usui. You seem to have a knack for collecting from the elderly, so I need you to make a quick run.": "",
  "Leave it to me, Boss. I was a total grandma's boy, so I know how to talk to old ladies.": "",
  "That hostess. She didn't take off with our money, did she? You know where her family lives, right?": "",
  "Yeah, I do... but I'm still gonna ask around a bit more.": "",
  "Hey, Shimura hasn't come in yet, has he?": "",
  "No, he's out collecting. He's been waiting in front of the client's house all night.": "",
  "Damn. Go make sure he's not bothering the neighbors.": "",
  "You know... I got my start as a lender working somewhere else. Real depressing place, that was.": "",
  "Seeing all those clients bump themselves off rather than live a life mired in debt... Got so sick of it, I ended up going solo.": "",
  "That hostess who ran out on her debt... I heard she's been working at another cabaret club nearby.": "",
  "Heh, she's either got ice in her veins or air in her brain. Either way, it didn't take much to get the money back.": "",
  "...You want something?": "",
  "Oh, no. Nothing in particular.": "",
  "...Then leave me the hell alone.": "",
  "(Guess that attitude is how he ended up here.)": "",
  "Well, if it ain't mister miracle man, the guy who saved my life!": "",
  "Eh, I was just in the right place at the right time. Glad to see you're up and about, Kondo-san.": "",
  "I donated blood to you, y'know. That means you owe me.": "",
  "That's a donation, not a debt! Besides, I couldn't pay ya back even if I tried!": "",
  "Haha, well. You could always return the favor if Fukuhara-san ever gets hurt.": "",
  "Yeah, and with interest on top of it. <font_kind=yakuza_italic>High</font_kind> interest.": "",
  "Sheesh. If only I knew my donor was out for more blood than he was willing to give.": "",
  "Well, if it isn't good ol' Yagami-san. What brings you here, anyway? You bored?": "",
  "Not as bored as you guys.": "",
  "Hey, I got all sortsa stuff to do. Even though it might not look that way.": "",
  "Oh yeah? What kinda stuff?": "",
  "I collect cans at night. And every morning at five, I'll wake up and collect magazines.": "",
  "Damn, that's pretty early.": "",
  "Early bird gets the worm. There's a lotta competition on the streets.": "",
  "...Guess I take my lifestyle for granted. I can pretty much eat and sleep as early or late as I want. Usually it's late.": "",
  "Heh. What an easygoing life you must have.": "",
  "Tell me about it. There was this one time I got so drunk, I pretty much slept two days in a row... It was amazing.": "",
  "...I might not be the most qualified person to be giving out advice, but I think you should be doing more with your life.": "",
  "Thanks for the warning...": "",
  "Hey, Kondo-san. How'd you... you know... end up on the streets?": "",
  "Hmm, now there's a question...": "",
  "I probably just got sick and tired of the nagging, the pressure, and all the frustrating responsibilites of family life.": "",
  "People you love can hurt you, y'know. The folks out here are much easier to deal with.": "",
  "I gotta say, Kon-chan looks much better since coming here. When I first saw him, he looked like a walking corpse!": "",
  "Really? I did? Heh... No fibbing, I wasn't even sure why I was alive back then.": "",
  "All I remember is everything felt like hell. And now look at me. It ain't much, but this's my little slice of heaven.": "",
  "So you found somewhere to belong, huh? Wish I could say the same.": "",
  "Then how about joining us, Yagami-san? Whaddya say?": "",
  "If this detective thing doesn't pan out, then maybe... Heck, at least I'd have a senpai.": "",
  "Ahoy there, Yagami-san. How's the working man's life?": "",
  "Yeah, got any interesting tales to tell?": "",
  "I do, actually. Just the other day, I was asked to find a cat that was supposedly worth billions of yen...": "",
  "Hoho... Now that's a story alright. So, what happened next?": "",
  "Huh. So you stumbled upon a secret hideout, eh?": "",
  "H-Hey, I used to feed that cat! Until I lost track of it.": "",
  "Argh... I knew its collar looked expensive, too...": "",
  "Damn it all! Was I <font_kind=yakuza_italic>this</font_kind> close to becoming a billionaire!?": "",
  "I'm not so sure about that... Then again, you never know...": "",
  "Interesting, to say the least. You know about the Twisted Trio?": "",
  "Yeah, I do! I've seen 'em a few times now!": "",
  "Yeah, ain't that right, Kon-chan? Remember that naked guy with the mask?": "",
  "Yep! Saw the whole thing, didn't we? And I mean the <font_kind=yakuza_italic>whole thing</font_kind>.": "",
  "Really? Where'd you see him last?": "",
  "Hotel District, back alley. But man... You shoulda seen the size of his pecker. This dude had some <font_kind=yakuza_italic>magnitude</font_kind>.": "",
  "Was he really that big?": "",
  "Big doesn't even begin to describe it. His dangus nearly dangled to the ground. It was like the Statue of David on steroids.": "",
  "What a monster...": "",
  "He certainly was a work of art if I've ever seen one. No wonder people worship him as the Exhibitionist Emperor.": "",
  "Hmm. Guess I'd have to see it to believe it... Not that I want to.": "",
  "Hey, we need to talk.": "",
  "Yagami-san? Sure, what's going on?": "",
  "Did you guys know about the gun trade the Keihin Gang were running?": "",
  "Yeah. Sorry we couldn't do anything to help.": "",
  "They threatened us. They said they'd kill us all if we let anything slip about the hideout.": "",
  "What were Onodera-san and Moroboshi-san doing this whole time?": "",
  "Ah, those two did what they always do.": "",
  "Moroboshi-sensei said all are equal before the scalpel, and patched up the injured Keihin Gang members.": "",
  "Meanwhile, Onodera-san was mumbling about how interesting an experience this was. He just watched from the corner.": "",
  "Haha, sounds just like them.": "",
  "Hey, Kondo-san. I got something you might like.": "",
  "What's this, a shogi board?": "",
  "Yeah. Wanna play sometime?": "",
  "Sure, but where? We'd only get in the way if played in the park.": "",
  "How about the sewers? Ain't no one down there to complain.": "",
  "Ooh, that's a good idea. Let's do that, then.": "",
  "Oh yeah, you're good at shogi, right? What was that thing you did?": "",
  "You know, all those shogi problems you gave us to solve.": "",
  "Yeah yeah. You should try it for yourself.": "",
  "Oh, you mean puzzle shogi. Yeah, I suppose I could try it sometime.": "",
  "You hungry, Yagami-san? 'Cause I got an extra bento over here.": "",
  "You got that from behind a convenience store, didn't you?": "",
  "Well, sure. But they're surprisingly edible, y'know. Bentos these days are fulla preservatives, so they don't go bad.": "",
  "Uh-huh. Well, I appreciate the offer, but no thanks.": "",
  "Ahoy there. Making good money these days?": "",
  "Then how bouts I introduce you to a gig? Help me pick up some cans.": "",
  "Your reward will be a delicious luxury yakiniku bento. One I scrounged up, that is.": "",
  "Haha. Tempting. But unfortunately I don't have that kind of time. Detective business, you understand.": "",
  "Didn't fall for it, huh.": "",
  "Of course not. Don't be lazy and go do it yourself.": "",
  "Yagami-san, do you smell something? I ain't talkin' my regular body odor, either. It's more like rancid diarrhea.": "",
  "Yep, that was me. I sorta cut the cheese.": "",
  "Seriously!? What kinda food did ya eat to make your farts smell so god-awful!?": "",
  "Ohh... oogh... ughhh... Hoo boy... I feel another one comin'!": "",
  "You better sniff it all up yourself, or else people are gonna file a complaint!": "",
  "So my buddy was cooking some meat, so I'm thinkin', \"Of course I'm gonna have some!\" Well... turns out it was a baby snake.": "",
  "Aww, no! I actually ate some of that shit, man! I thought it was fried chicken!": "",
  "Yagami-san, guess what! I stumbled across this rare magazine the other day...": "",
  "Sold that thing for twenty grand! You never know which porno mag is worth something. Remember that.": "",
  "Goddammit! Stupid net café employee kicked me out!": "",
  "You do smell pretty bad. Use the public restroom and clean yourself up.": "",
  "Being homeless is pretty awesome, you know. No taxes and no work.": "",
  "Yagami-san. There's this place in the rich part of town where they throw away valuable stuff.": "",
  "I found a watch that costs 800,000 yen last time. Too bad I can't tell ya where.": "",
  "Huh? You need something, dude?": "",
  "Oh, no. Sorry.": "",
  "(Another host done with a hard day's work. I probably shouldn't bug him.)": "",
  "Heeeey! Yagami-san!": "",
  "Ah, Deguchi-san. Are you off work now?": "",
  "Yeah, I was just grabbing something to eat with my boys.": "",
  "Huh, so this is the famous Yagami-san?": "",
  "So he's the one who beat Deguchi in a pickup battle?": "",
  "Yep, that actually happened.": "",
  "Incredible. Maybe you'd be a better host than Deguchi.": "",
  "H-Hey, I still have plenty of room to improve!": "",
  "And you're gonna be the number one host in Kamurocho, right?": "",
  "More like number one nutsack. You're still below average, even with the makeover.": "",
  "\"Man looks at the outward appearance, but a host is judged by the heart.\" Isn't that how the saying goes?": "",
  "...I don't know what you're talking about, but good luck. Try not to end up on that tuna boat.": "",
  "R-Right! That's the plan!": "",
  "Oh... what's up, Yagami-san...": "",
  "Hey, is everything all right? You look a little down.": "",
  "Yeah, something's been on my mind...": "",
  "So one of my customers started requesting me specifically. She's even dropped my name at the club.": "",
  "Isn't that a good thing?": "",
  "...No, Yagami-san. Do you know what \"bombing\" is?": "",
  "Is that some sort of host thing?": "",
  "Yeah. It's when a host contacts a girl who already has a designated host. Basically, it's poaching someone else's client.": "",
  "In our industry, taking clients from each other is the worst thing you can do. They'll even fine your ass for it.": "",
  "I guess that would be problematic, especially when your livelihood depends on it.": "",
  "Right. So there's a rumor going around that one of my girls has been texting another guy at the club.": "",
  "I can see why you'd be worried about that. But is this rumor true?": "",
  "I'm not sure yet.": "",
  "Well, why don't you wait and see what happens?": "",
  "I suppose that's all I can do...": "",
  "Deguchi-san. Did you ever find out what was going on with your customer?": "",
  "Oh, about that. Actually, it's kind of a weird story.": "",
  "Weird? How so?": "",
  "The host that was contacting my customer... It turns out he's her brother.": "",
  "What the heck? They were siblings?": "",
  "Yeah. Apparently, he's been trying to convince her to stop visiting the club 'cause she's married.": "",
  "So you had nothing to worry about after all.": "",
  "Ahaha, yeah. She was my first regular customer, so I guess I panicked a little.": "",
  "You know, come to think of it...": "",
  "You were actually able to win the heart of a married woman. Doesn't that mean you've improved at being a host?": "",
  "Hey, it's as I keep saying. I know how to keep the conversation real.": "",
  "Well, I wish you the best of luck.": "",
  "Yagami-san! You're safe!": "",
  "Yeah. Thanks to you.": "",
  "I saw it on the news. The police arrested all the gun smugglers.": "",
  "That was your doing, right?": "",
  "Crazy people won't be waving around guns in Kamurocho anymore. You're a hero, Yagami-san.": "",
  "A guy with a bounty on his head becomes a hero the next day. What a story.": "",
  "How's your host thing going, Deguchi-san?": "",
  "Not very good. I'm still just a helper.": "",
  "Well, you'll just have to work hard and take it one step at a time.": "",
  "Yeah! I'll make both you and my auntie proud!": "",
  "Dang, look at you, player! That's a sick jacket right there! You really got style, my dude!": "",
  "Whoa, where are all these compliments coming from?": "",
  "I'm practicing giving out compliments! You know, for the ladies.": "",
  "Oh, I see. Does it help to compliment guys, too?": "",
  "It's the same thing, really, in the sense that I'm trying to make people happy.": "",
  "I see. Well, do your best.": "",
  "Apparently this host at White Tiger booked it because he couldn't pay his customer's tab.": "",
  "Damn. I should be careful not to let my customer's tab rack up too high.": "",
  "Yagami-san, don't you get lonely when it's cold out like this? I want to date a girl outside of work sometime.": "",
  "I went to a party last night, and a girl busted out laughing when I told her I was a host...": "",
  "I wonder what was so funny.": "",
  "Don't you think I look like that one idol, Kento Amahara? Thank my parents for these amazing genetics.": "",
  "Can't believe how freakin' expensive these champagne towers are. This customer dropped 1.2 million like it was nothing.": "",
  "Psh, I've seen someone drop 8 million before. Hard to believe our economy's in a slump with that kinda money floating around.": "",
  "Host clubs can be a pretty scary place. There was a customer last night who dropped two million.": "",
  "She wasn't my customer though...": "",
  "A surprising amount of younger girls come to host clubs, too.": "",
  "Some of them are definitely in college. I'm worried that they might be going bankrupt.": "",
  "This customer said she wanted to take a picture with me, so I went along with it.": "",
  "Then one of my coworkers showed me that very same picture on Chatter with the message, \"Look at his huge face! L-O-L.\"": "",
  "Hey, you can't just come in here!": "",
  "Ah. My bad.": "",
  "(I've been scolded...)": "",
  "Hey, what's the good word?": "",
  "Oh, aren't you... Yagami-san?": "",
  "Yeah, you're the Battle of the Alps champion the manager's always talking about.": "",
  "Yeah. We were just talking about the challenge and how none of us, including the customers, would ever wanna do it.": "",
  "Our manager's a real coffee nut, so it's pretty hard to keep up with him.": "",
  "Haha, I see.": "",
  "But I guess that worked in his favor when that yakuza-looking dude stopped by the other day.": "",
  "Yeah, that was a tricky situation.": "",
  "Here, have a seat, Yagami-san. Coffee's on me today.": "",
  "(Wow. Coffee, free of charge. How nice.)": "",
  "Ah, it's a pleasure to see you, Yagami-sama.": "",
  "Hey, Sagara-san. What's new?": "",
  "I just bought a rare type of coffee today.": "",
  "Do you know about Geisha?": "",
  "Geisha? Like the ones in Kyoto?": "",
  "No, no. Not that geisha. It's a type of coffee bean.": "",
  "It's from a place called Geisha in Ethiopia, and it's considered to be one of the best coffees in the world.": ""
 },
 "ref_tm": {
  "You serious?": "เอาจริงเหรอ?",
  "I'm not sure yet.": "ยังไม่แน่ใจ"
 }
}
